": 1197.5, "width": 102.20000000000005, "height": 201.0999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "O (0) 12 (0)", "bbox": {"x": 804.6, "y": 983.5, "width": 67.10000000000002, "height": 61.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "O (0) 25 (100)", "bbox": {"x": 807.8, "y": 1088.5, "width": 86.20000000000005, "height": 61.100000000000136}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "1(3) 0 (0) 14 (26)", "bbox": {"x": 807.8, "y": 1197.5, "width": 73.39999999999998, "height": 92.90000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "12（80） 2 (33) 66 (30)", "bbox": {"x": 804.6, "y": 1306.1, "width": 79.79999999999995, "height": 92.60000000000014}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "10 （77） 0 (0) 0（0） 28 (100) 0 (0) 0 (0) 1 (3) 0（0） 14 (26) 0 (0) 4 (67) 57 (26)", "bbox": {"x": 996.2, "y": 983.5, "width": 92.69999999999982, "height": 415.0999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "3 (13) 0 (0) O (0)", "bbox": {"x": 1149.5, "y": 983.5, "width": 67.09999999999991, "height": 96.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "25 (100) 7 (100) 28 (90) 13 (100) 25 (46) 7 (47) 0 (0)", "bbox": {"x": 1143.1, "y": 1127.2, "width": 86.5, "height": 233.20000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "108 (49)", "bbox": {"x": 1127.1, "y": 1376.3, "width": 89.40000000000009, "height": 26.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "O (0) 12 (100) 17 (100) ७() O (0) 0(0) 2 (7) O (0) 14 (26) 8 (53) 2 (33) 55 (25)", "bbox": {"x": 1334.7, "y": 983.5, "width": 93.69999999999982, "height": 415.0999999999999}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(p = 0.0453, odds ratio, OR = 2.289 (1.018-5.150)) (Fig. 4). There was no statistically significant difference in the clinical outcome between type II and type III knee dislocations.", "bbox": {"x": 137.1, "y": 1478.3, "width": 667.6, "height": 132.9000000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Discussion", "bbox": {"x": 137.3, "y": 1689.1, "width": 131.0, "height": 25.799999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The most important finding of the presented study is that suture repair of cruciate ligaments leads to similar clinical results than cruciate ligament reconstruction in multiligament injuries of the knee. As shown in our study, good and excellent results were achieved by suture repair of the ACL and PCL in 77.5% of patients with type III and IV knee", "bbox": {"x": 137.3, "y": 1756.2, "width": 670.5, "height": 204.89999999999986}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "dislocations, according to Schenck's classification [23]. These clinical results are comparable to those accomplished by ligament reconstruction. A major problem of most published articles about knee dislocations is the lack of homogeneity in injury pattern, as well as the variety of different treatment regimens. As shown in our study the injury pattern according to Schenck has a significant influence on the clinical outcome. Former meta-analyses of knee dislocations did not consider the severity and pattern of the injury [3, 11]. To our knowledge, this study is the first meta-analysis of knee dislocations based on individual patient data with the possibility of matching patients to distinct injury patterns to obtain more homogeneous treatment groups.", "bbox": {"x": 843.0, "y": 1478.3, "width": 670.7, "height": 482.79999999999995}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "2) Springer", "bbox": {"x": 1390.9, "y": 2050.1, "width": 123.20000000000005, "height": 33.5}}], "ms": 226.75}